From: UAF Injection Patch 002
Subject: [PATCH] UAF in jdmarker.c: freed JHUFF_TBL on DHT table redefinition

Vulnerability type : Use-After-Free
File               : jdmarker.c
Function           : get_dht
Trigger            : A JPEG stream that contains TWO DHT markers defining
                     the SAME table class (tc=0, DC) and the SAME destination
                     id (th=0).  The second DHT marker must have bits[1]==0x00
                     AND bits[2]==0x00 (zero 1-bit and zero 2-bit codes).
                     This is legal JPEG but unusual — standard tables have
                     bits[2]>=1.
Difficulty         : Medium for AFL++ — the DHT marker bytes need mutation
                     beyond what standard tables provide.  bits[2] must be
                     zeroed (standard DC tables have bits[2]==1, AC tables
                     have bits[2]==2), requiring a targeted byte mutation.

The injection: when get_dht sees that the destination slot already holds a
non-NULL pointer AND bits[1] == 0, it calls free() on the existing JHUFF_TBL
directly (bypassing the memory pool), then overwrites the slot pointer with a
fresh pool allocation.  Any cached pointer to the old table (e.g., the one
saved in d_derived_tbl structures built from the previous scan) now dangles.
jpeg_make_d_derived_tbl uses that pointer as 'htbl' and reads htbl->bits[].

Adapted for libjpeg-turbo 2.1.3: the local variable is htblptr (JHUFF_TBL **)
rather than htbl (JHUFF_TBL *), so the condition and free use *htblptr.
bits[1] is used directly (already read into the bits[] array) instead of
GETJOCTET(p[0]).

--- a/jdmarker.c
+++ b/jdmarker.c
@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@
 #define JPEG_INTERNALS
 #include "jinclude.h"
 #include "jpeglib.h"
+#include <stdlib.h>
 
 
 typedef enum {                  /* JPEG marker codes */
@@ -488,6 +489,28 @@ get_dht(j_decompress_ptr cinfo)
       htblptr = &cinfo->dc_huff_tbl_ptrs[index];
     }
 
+    /*
+     * BUG INJECTION (UAF-002):
+     * When redefining an already-populated Huffman table slot, free the
+     * existing JHUFF_TBL via stdlib free() rather than returning it to the
+     * memory pool.  The pool still considers the allocation live; any
+     * d_derived_tbl that caches a pointer to the old table will read freed
+     * memory during the first Huffman decode after this marker.
+     *
+     * Trigger: bits[1] (first DHT count) must be 0x00, and the slot must
+     * already be non-NULL (i.e., previously defined in a prior DHT marker).
+     */
+#ifndef MAGMA_ENABLE_FIXES
+#ifdef MAGMA_ENABLE_CANARIES
+    MAGMA_LOG("JPGUAF02", *htblptr != NULL && bits[1] == 0x00 && bits[2] == 0x00);
+#endif
+    if (*htblptr != NULL && bits[1] == 0x00 && bits[2] == 0x00) {
+      /* Directly free the pool-allocated table — dangling refs remain */
+      free(*htblptr);
+      *htblptr = NULL;  /* slot will be reallocated below, but cached ptrs dangle */
+    }
+#endif
+
     if (*htblptr == NULL)
       *htblptr = jpeg_alloc_huff_table((j_common_ptr)cinfo);
 
